{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01GhfjQgiwE4mpk52xB9PYEV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the research context carefully to define three tiers of Dream scenarios for this FREIGE project targeting EMNLP 2026 Main.\n\nKey facts from the context:\n\n**Current MVP results:**\n- SFT baseline: rel_f1=0.4057, evi_f1=0.7979, EDCR=0.7118\n- RSFT+CED best (s43_r2): rel_f1=0.4683, evi_f1=0.8156, EDCR=0.6388\n- RSFT+CED range: rel_f1=0.4449-0.4683, evi_f1=0.8087-0.8187, EDCR=0.6350-0.6641\n\n\n- GRPO shows severe catastrophic forgetting with relation F1 dropping below 0.02 at optimal learning rates\n\n**Key upcoming experiments:**\n1. plan_001: CED vs flat-NLI RSFT ablation (P0) - critical for Claim 2\n2. plan_002: Test set evaluation\n3. plan_004: DREEAM baseline reproduction\n4. plan_011: GRPO G=8 experiment\n5. plan_012: DPO+CED experiment\n6. plan_013: EDCR human validation\n\n**Key risks identified in Dream:**\n- CED vs flat-NLI may not be significant (p>0.05) - all three tiers flagged this\n- G=4 too small for GRPO - all three tiers flagged this\n- Missing DPO baseline - M/W flagged\n- EDCR needs human validation - M/W flagged\n\n**Core claims:**\n1. CED-scored RSFT enables simultaneous extraction + faithful evidence\n2. CED scoring > flat-NLI scoring for RSFT\n3. GRPO+QLoRA catastrophic forgetting with evidence-extraction decoupling\n4. EDCR as independent evaluation metric\n\nNow I'm thinking through the best-case scenario where all hypotheses hold up: CED outperforms flat-NLI with statistical significance, test set results remain stable or improve, GRPO G=8 still exhibits catastrophic forgetting to strengthen the decoupling claim, and DPO shows intermediate performance between the two approaches.\n\nFor the median case, the CED advantage might not reach significance, test margins could shrink, but GRPO's failure persists and EDCR shows moderate human correlation. In the worst case, CED shows no meaningful difference from flat-NLI, test gains drop below 2 percentage points, GRPO G=8 partially recovers which would undermine the catastrophic forgetting claim, and EDCR fails to correlate with human judgment.\n\nNow I'm looking at the specific numbers on the dev set to ground these scenarios. Looking at the GRPO results with G=8, the outcomes span from catastrophic forgetting in the best case to substantial improvements in the worst case, which would require reframing my claims about the approach. For EDCR human validation, I'm seeing correlation ranges from strong agreement above 0.6 down to weak correlation below 0.3. With DPO, the best scenario shows intermediate performance that creates a clean spectrum story between online and offline methods, though the median case would blur that distinction.\n\nNow I'm working through the precise number ranges to establish what constitutes success—test relative F1 scores in the 0.44-0.48 range would hold my development results and exceed SFT by a meaningful margin, while evidence F1 should land competitively around 0.50-0.55 accounting for the joint evaluation protocol. I'm also tracking the effect sizes for CED versus flat-NLI, looking for statistical significance in both the evidence metrics and the EDCR differences.\n\nBut I'm realizing I need to be more careful about how the evaluation protocol affects these numbers—the current conditional evidence F1 scores around 0.80 are computed differently than the DREEAM joint protocol that gives 57.34 on test, so switching protocols will likely produce substantially lower numbers than what I've been seeing in development. ) will compute evidence F1 differently - it's joint with relation extraction, so only correct relations' evidence counts.\n\nGiven rel_f1 ~0.40-0.47 and conditional evi_f1 ~0.80-0.82, the joint evi_f1 would be much lower. DREEAM's 57.34 is on test set. Let me estimate...\n\nActually, DREEAM's 57.34 is Evi-F1 (joint) which counts evidence only for correctly predicted relations. Given that FREIGE's rel_f1 is ~0.40-0.47 while DREEAM/encoder models have higher rel_f1 (DREEAM uses RoBERTa-large), the joint Evi-F1 will be scaled by the relation recall.\n\nBut wait - this is complex. The joint Evi-F1 depends on how many relations are correctly identified AND how good the evidence is for those correct relations. With FREIGE's rel_f1 around 0.45 versus encoder models hitting 0.60+, FREIGE identifies fewer correct relations overall, but the evidence quality for those it does catch is quite strong at around 0.82 conditional F1. So the joint score would roughly be the product of these: 0.45 × 0.82 ≈ 0.37, putting FREIGE in the 0.30-0.40 range on dev under the new protocol. DREEAM's 57.34 also reflects this product of relation and evidence performance, though its attention-based approach makes direct comparison tricky. The real takeaway is that FREIGE appears to be the first LM-based method producing evidence at all, so comparing variants against each other and against SFT baseline matters more than the DREEAM reference point.\n\nNow I need to structure the YAML focusing on the metrics that actually matter: test rel_f1 with improvement over SFT, joint evi_f1, CED versus flat-NLI significance, GRPO with G=8 results, EDCR human correlation, and DPO outcomes. I should also account for the D042 corrections narrowing Claim 3 to GRPO+QLoRA, the planned GRPO G=8 experiment, and the DPO baseline work.\n\nDefining the key metrics for number_ranges...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20220,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20220},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c60a310b-24a8-4db5-ab3a-ef401c18461b","uuid":"fdbaf551-a11d-4132-a63c-b836b565de78"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01GhfjQgiwE4mpk52xB9PYEV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"所有核心假设成立：CED 显著优于 flat-NLI，test set 保持 dev 增幅，GRPO G=8 仍崩，DPO 填补光谱，EDCR 人工验证通过\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"CED vs flat-NLI RSFT 在 evi_f1 和 EDCR 上均显著（p<0.01），对比性 margin 确实过滤了 distractor-heavy 候选\"\n      - \"Test set rel_f1 Δ ≥ +3.5pp over SFT（dev→test 退化 ≤1.5pp），evi_f1_joint 在 DREEAM 对齐协议下仍优于 SFT\"\n      - \"GRPO G=8 仍 catastrophic forgetting（rel_f1 < 0.05），排除 advantage estimation noise 作为 G=4 失败的混淆因素\"\n      - \"DPO+CED 不崩但弱于 RSFT（rel_f1 0.25-0.38），形成 online→offline 清晰退化光谱\"\n      - \"EDCR 与人工判断 Pearson r ≥ 0.55，验证其作为自动指标的有效性\"\n      - \"DREEAM baseline 可复现（Evi-F1 ≈ 57.34），FREIGE 的 joint Evi-F1 在 LLM 方法中无可比对手\"\n    number_ranges:\n      test_rel_f1_delta_over_sft: [3.5, 6.5]     # pp, SFT test baseline ~0.39-0.41\n      ced_vs_flatnli_evi_f1_delta: [1.5, 3.0]     # pp, CED RSFT 优于 flat-NLI RSFT\n      ced_vs_flatnli_edcr_delta: [-8.0, -4.0]     # pp, CED 更低=更好\n      ced_vs_flatnli_p_value: [0.001, 0.01]\n      grpo_g8_best_rel_f1: [0.00, 0.05]\n      dpo_rel_f1: [0.25, 0.38]\n      edcr_human_pearson_r: [0.55, 0.75]\n      rsft_best_test_rel_f1: [0.43, 0.48]\n      rsft_test_evi_f1_joint: [0.34, 0.42]        # joint 协议下显著低于 conditional\n    narrative_direction: >\n      原始 framing 完全成立。四个 Claims 全部有强证据支撑：\n      C1（首个同时生成抽取+证据的 LLM DocRE）有 test set 显著优势；\n      C2（CED > flat-NLI）有统计显著性；\n      C3（GRPO+QLoRA decoupling）有 G=4 和 G=8 双重验证 + DPO 中间点对比；\n      C4（EDCR 指标）有人工标注背书。\n      论文可用完整的 \"problem → naive reward fails → online RL fails → CED+RSFT solves it\" story arc，\n      无需降级任何 claim。主表可展示完整的 online-offline 光谱（GRPO → DPO → RSFT）。\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"核心方法有效但 CED 优势不显著：RSFT 整体优于 SFT 但 CED vs flat-NLI p>0.05，GRPO G=8 仍崩，EDCR 人工验证中等\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"CED vs flat-NLI RSFT 差异方向正确但不显著（Δevi_f1 0.3-1.2pp, p=0.05-0.20），CED 的对比性 margin 优势被 NLI 噪声稀释\"\n      - \"Test set rel_f1 Δ = +2.0-3.5pp over SFT（dev→test 退化 2-3pp），仍显著但幅度收窄\"\n      - \"GRPO G=8 仍崩（rel_f1 < 0.10），Claim 3 成立但需承认 full-rank 未测\"\n      - \"DPO 结果不够理想：要么也部分崩（rel_f1 0.10-0.25）要么接近 RSFT（rel_f1 0.40+），光谱不够清晰\"\n      - \"EDCR 与人工判断 r=0.35-0.55，有信号但不够强\"\n    number_ranges:\n      test_rel_f1_delta_over_sft: [2.0, 3.5]\n      ced_vs_flatnli_evi_f1_delta: [0.3, 1.5]\n      ced_vs_flatnli_edcr_delta: [-5.0, -1.0]\n      ced_vs_flatnli_p_value: [0.05, 0.20]\n      grpo_g8_best_rel_f1: [0.00, 0.10]\n      dpo_rel_f1: [0.10, 0.42]                    # 不确定性大：可能崩也可能太好\n      edcr_human_pearson_r: [0.35, 0.55]\n      rsft_best_test_rel_f1: [0.41, 0.45]\n      rsft_test_evi_f1_joint: [0.28, 0.36]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      触发 CED contingency plan：CED 从核心贡献降级为\"可选 scoring function\"。\n      论文重心转移到三条独立但互补的贡献：\n      (1) Claim 1 升格为主贡献——首个 evidence-generating LLM for DocRE，RSFT（无论用哪种 scorer）均显著优于 SFT；\n      (2) Claim 3 保持——GRPO+QLoRA decoupling phenomenon 作为 analysis contribution，但 DPO 部分需根据实际结果灵活处理；\n      (3) Claim 4 调整——EDCR 作为 diagnostic tool 而非 validated metric，报告人工相关性但坦诚局限。\n      CED vs flat-NLI 作为 ablation 诚实报告\"方向正确但未达显著\"，不作为 selling point。\n      叙事从 \"CED 是关键创新\" 转为 \"RSFT pipeline 是关键创新 + GRPO failure analysis 是独立贡献\"。\n      需要补充实验加强 Claim 1（如 model size ablation 或 Re-DocRED）弥补 CED claim 的弱化。\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"RSFT 优势在 test set 上大幅缩水，且 GRPO G=8 部分恢复，核心叙事需要全面 reframe\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"CED vs flat-NLI 无差异或 flat-NLI 略优（Δevi_f1 < 0.3pp），CED 的对比性设计在 RSFT 间接作用下无可观测效果\"\n      - \"Test set rel_f1 Δ ≤ +2.0pp over SFT（dev→test 退化 >3pp），可能不显著（p>0.05），dev 增幅存在过拟合成分\"\n      - \"GRPO G=8 部分恢复（rel_f1 0.15-0.30），说明 G=4 的失败有 advantage noise 成分，Claim 3 需大幅限定范围\"\n      - \"DPO rel_f1 ≥ 0.35，接近 RSFT，说明 offline 优势不在于 rejection sampling 而在于避免 policy gradient\"\n      - \"EDCR 与人工判断 r < 0.35，EDCR 作为独立指标的价值存疑\"\n    number_ranges:\n      test_rel_f1_delta_over_sft: [0.5, 2.0]\n      ced_vs_flatnli_evi_f1_delta: [-0.5, 0.3]\n      ced_vs_flatnli_edcr_delta: [-2.0, 2.0]\n      ced_vs_flatnli_p_value: [0.20, 0.80]\n      grpo_g8_best_rel_f1: [0.15, 0.30]           # 部分恢复\n      dpo_rel_f1: [0.35, 0.44]\n      edcr_human_pearson_r: [0.10, 0.35]\n      rsft_best_test_rel_f1: [0.39, 0.43]\n      rsft_test_evi_f1_joint: [0.22, 0.30]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      需要全面 reframe，但仍冲 EMNLP Main，不降级目标。Reframe 策略：\n      论文从 \"method paper\" 转型为 \"analysis + benchmark paper\"。\n      核心叙事变为：对 LLM DocRE 的 evidence generation 进行首次系统性研究，\n      回答 \"哪些 RL/training 策略能让 LLM 在文档级 IE 中生成可验证证据\" 这一开放问题。\n      贡献重组为：(1) 首个 LLM DocRE evidence benchmark（任务定义 + 评测协议 + 多指标框架）；\n      (2) online vs offline RL 的系统对比（GRPO vs DPO vs RSFT，含 G=4/G=8 消融），\n      发现不是 online RL 本身失败而是 QLoRA+小 group size 的脆弱组合；\n      (3) evidence 评估指标的局限性分析（Evi-F1 conditional vs joint 的差异 + EDCR 的信号与噪声）。\n      CED 完全降级为一种 explored scoring function。\n      需大幅增加实验覆盖（model sizes, datasets）来支撑 \"systematic study\" 叙事。\n      投稿可能推迟到 ARR September 或 AAAI 2027 以积累足够实验。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20220,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20220},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c60a310b-24a8-4db5-ab3a-ef401c18461b","uuid":"22909610-c816-410d-90e6-d5d3030967f9"}
